# ⛔ DO-NOT registry (hard stops)

**Before touching BG/collision registration, room identity, or any surface
named in [docs/DO-NOT.md](../../docs/DO-NOT.md): read the matching entry.**

- Entries are **permanent rejections**, not advice. Each documents a confirmed
  incident: the failure mechanism, the blast radius, and the sanctioned path.
- The failure class these guard is **invisible at the change site and loud
  everywhere else** — your own test will not show you the breakage.
- **No AI instance may self-approve an exception.** If you believe your case
  is genuinely different, write it up against the entry's mechanism
  point-by-point and get an explicit user go first.

Current entries: **DN-1** — never `SetRoomId(0)`/keep-slot/guessed room on
standable geometry (poisons the player's room → every room-keyed subsystem
fails: stage events, doors, camera; №256 incident).
